Q: Building a tree structure from a flat array A: <p>You don't need a stack or recursion, just remember the last items of levels to put children to them:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const arr = [
  {lv: 0, name: "A"},
  {lv: 1, name: "B"},
  {lv: 1, name: "C"},
  {lv: 2, name: "D"},
  {lv: 3, name: "E"},
  {lv: 1, name: "F"},
  {lv: 0, name: "G"},
]
const result = [], last = [{children: result}]; // collect last nodes of levels
for(const {lv, name} of arr){
  const node = {name, children: null};
  (last[lv].children ??= []).push(node);
  last[lv + 1] = node;
}

console.log(result);</code></pre>
